---
import Case from '../../layouts/Case.astro';

// Draft wording, for the owner to review before publishing.
const glance: [string, string][] = [
  ['What', 'A study aid'],
  ['Built with', 'Claude'],
  ['Status', 'In use, unofficial'],
  ['Shown', 'Live, in your browser'],
];
---

<Case title="C⁴ study guide" glance={glance} link="https://nao-mei.github.io/c4-study/" linkLabel="Open the study guide">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <h1>C⁴ <span class="mut">study guide</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A study aid for Claude's certification exams, built with Claude's help. I used it to pass the Claude Certified Developer – Foundations and Architect – Professional exams.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>Where it started</h2>
  <p>
    I was preparing for Claude's certification exams myself, and wanted a study aid I could keep improving as I went.
  </p>

  <h2>What I did</h2>
  <p>
    I built the guide with Claude's help. It runs entirely in your browser: no accounts, and nothing is sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Did it work?</h2>
  <p>
    I used it to prepare for the Claude Certified Developer – Foundations and Architect – Professional exams, and passed both. I keep using it for the exams that follow.
  </p>

  <h2>Honest by design</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It is unofficial, and says so before you start.</li>
    <li>It was drafted with AI, and says that too, so you know to check it against the official material.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What I learned</h2>
  <p>
    The best study tool is one that shows you your own gaps. Building it taught me as much as using it, and doing both is why I trust it.
  </p>
</Case>
